not three new rules and not three independent proof classes.

| Setting | Source/proof result | Final disposition |
|---|---|---|
| Whole-constant-run relabelling on $[n]^n$ (WCR) | Complete author proof: fixed Carlitz core; sharp full-carrier height $1+\lfloor\log_2 n\rfloor$ for $n\geq2$, zero at $n=1$; every-target one-step inverse, image size $2^{n-1}$, and every-size maximum-fibre equality cases. | `KILL_VALUE_NO_SEPARATE_SECOND_RESIDUAL`: temporal core is ordered positive-mass merging with causal doubling. All inverse freedom is proper colouring of a forced path segmentation; fixed enumeration is classical Carlitz. |
| Rooted/ordered tree reductions | Full text of the 12-page Horton/register extended abstract read; it explicitly defines leaf deletion plus unary suppression and states exact register descent. Original LGB full proof also supplies an already rejected potential/local-inverse tree example. | `DESK_KILL_OWNED_REDUCTION_OR_THIN_LOCAL_MOVE`. No new tree rule is counted. Extended-abstract omitted proofs remain uninspected; no full-primary-proof claim. |
| Set-partition crossing/size-merging settings | Original CCQ and sixth partition-lane notes identify classical noncrossing closure and expressly excluded equal-size merging. Search metadata is supporting navigation only. | `DESK_KILL_OLD_CLOSURE_OR_MERGER_MOTIF`. No new partition literal, theorem extension or source clearance. |

## The concrete theorem progress

[PROOF_PACKAGE.md](PROOF_PACKAGE.md) proves WCR deductively before any
code. If $R(x)$ is its ordered run-length composition and
$\Psi(b_1,\ldots,b_k)=b_1^{b_1}\cdots b_k^{b_k}$, then

$$F=\Psi R,\qquad R\Psi=M,\qquad F\Psi=\Psi M,$$

where $M$ merges every maximal adjacent group of equal masses. $\Psi$ is
injective. Every merger at epoch $t\geq2$ has an input created at epoch
$t-1$, so the resulting mass is at least $2^t$. Geometric compositions,
with a separate placement of the residual $2^{k-1}$, make the resulting
word-time bound sharp at every size.

For a target with maximal constant runs $a_j^{L_j}$, the fibre is empty
unless each $a_j$ divides $L_j$. Otherwise its source-run segmentation is
unique, with $K=\sum_j L_j/a_j$ blocks, and the complete fibre has
$n(n-1)^{K-1}$ words. For $n\geq3$ the unique maximum target is $1^n$;
the $n=1,2$ exceptions are included. This is fully evaluated, but it has
no extra combinatorial mechanism after path-colouring is deducted.

These are new author deductions in this package, not claims of priority
or independent review. The correct temporal theorem is preserved instead
of being labelled an admission. No second residual survives the source
and elementary-adapter subtraction, so the at-most-one-pilot allowance
is left unused. There is no canonical numerical output to replay and no
numerical all-size extrapolation.

